/-
    Path: {% include '~/Themes/GreaterThingsV1/Assets/Lava/Custom/Templates/Separator.lava', settings:separatorSettings %}
    Description: The join between two sections. A separator is decoration rather than content, so it
                 takes no height of its own: it is a zero height line sitting on the boundary, with the
                 shape centered on it so half falls in the section above and half in the one below.
                 Adding one never moves anything on the page.

                 Because it paints over both neighbors, the colors it is given have to be the
                 colors of those two sections. Nothing here can read them.

    Parameters:
        settings - Dictionary of the template settings. Keys:
            separator.type      - Which transition to draw. (Optional, ripped | gradient | fade.
                                  Defaults to ripped)
                                  ripped   - A torn paper edge. The section below appears to tear into
                                             the one above.
                                  gradient - A vertical fade from one section's color into the other's.
                                  fade     - One color at full strength on the join, falling away to
                                             nothing in both directions. Use it to haze a single color
                                             across a boundary without naming either section's color.

            separator.color     - ripped and fade: the single color. For ripped that is the tear, which
                                  is normally the background of the section below; for fade it is the
                                  color that peaks on the join. (Optional, Text. Defaults to the
                                  theme's pale interface color for ripped, and to transparent -- that
                                  is, nothing drawn -- for fade)

            separator.fromcolor - gradient only: the color at the top, normally the background of the
                                  section above. Leave it blank, or pass transparent, for a fade that
                                  rises out of whatever is already there -- useful over an image, or
                                  when only one of the two sections has a color worth naming.
                                  (Optional, Text. Defaults to transparent)
            separator.tocolor   - gradient only: the color at the bottom, normally the background of
                                  the section below. Blank or transparent behaves as above.
                                  (Optional, Text. Defaults to transparent)
            separator.height    - gradient and fade: how tall the fade is. Half of it falls either side
                                  of the join. (Optional, CSS length. Defaults to 120px)
-/

//- MARK: Settings Logic
{% assign separatorType = settings.separator.type | Default:'ripped' %}

{% assign fromColor = settings.separator.fromcolor | Default:'transparent' %}
{% assign toColor = settings.separator.tocolor | Default:'transparent' %}
{% assign fadeClass = '' %}
{% if separatorType == 'gradient' %}
    {% if fromColor != 'transparent' and toColor == 'transparent' %}
        {% assign fadeClass = ' fade-out' %}
    {% elsif fromColor == 'transparent' and toColor != 'transparent' %}
        {% assign fadeClass = ' fade-in' %}
    {% endif %}
{% endif %}

{% capture separatorStyles %}
    {% if settings.separator.color != blank %}--separator-color: {{ settings.separator.color }};{% endif %}
    {% if settings.separator.fromcolor != blank %}--separator-from-color: {{ settings.separator.fromcolor }};{% endif %}
    {% if settings.separator.tocolor != blank %}--separator-to-color: {{ settings.separator.tocolor }};{% endif %}
    {% if settings.separator.height != blank %}--separator-height: {{ settings.separator.height }};{% endif %}
{% endcapture %}
{% assign separatorStyles = separatorStyles | Trim %}

//- MARK: Markup
<div class="separator-template separator-{{ separatorType }}{{ fadeClass }}" style="{{ separatorStyles }}" aria-hidden="true">
    <div class="separator-inner">
        {% if separatorType == 'ripped' %}
            {% include '~/Themes/GreaterThingsV1/Assets/Images/Textures/RippedSeperator.lava', fill:settings.separator.color %}
        {% endif %}
        //- gradient and fade are the element itself. Nothing to draw.
    </div>
</div>
